// Tasks whose timers have expired join the run queue in the order of their
// deadlines (spec/04-semantics.md, Scheduling). `late` calls sleep() first, with
// the longer time, and `early` second, with the shorter time. `early` wakes
// first.
// The CHECK lines do not bind the bootstrap interpreter. It runs every worker on
// one host thread, so a blocking call blocks every task (spec/README.md,
// Conformance: scheduling is implementation-defined). The probe on the
// NOT-BINDING line checks the bootstrap's own choice in its place.
// STATUS: ok
// TIMEOUT: 10
// NOT-BINDING: bootstrap bootstrap-only/same_worker_blocking_call.lox
// CHECK: early woke
// CHECK: late woke
var me = task.self();
fun late() { sleep(0.4); print "late woke"; task.send(me, "done"); }
fun early() { sleep(0.1); print "early woke"; task.send(me, "done"); }
task.spawn(late);
task.spawn(early);
task.receive();
task.receive();
